    "NUMBER": "032",
    "SERIES": "2026-Q1 Babel",
    "WORD": "EVIL",
    "GLOSS": "Morally wrong, wicked, harmful; or, disaster, calamity, and misfortune.",
    "CARD_TYPE": "ADJECTIVE",
    "RARITY_TEXT": "UNCOMMON",
    "RARITY_ICON": "UNCOMMON",
    "ART_PROMPT": "A pristine white marble surface marred by a dark, jagged, spreading fissure that looks like a vein of corruption. Abstract and ominous, high contrast.",
    "ABILITY_TEXT": "Target player discards 1 card. If they have more cards in hand than you, they discard 2 instead.",
    "STAT_LORE": 4,
    "STAT_CONTEXT": 4,
    "STAT_COMPLEXITY": 2,
    "OT_VERSE_REF": "Isaiah 45:7 (KJV)",
    "OT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "I form the light, and create darkness: I make peace, and create evil: I the LORD do all these things.",
    "NT_VERSE_REF": "Matthew 6:13",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom...",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Isaiah 45:7 (KJV) — “I form the light, and create darkness: I make peace, and create evil: I the LORD do all these things.”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "Matthew 6:13 — “And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom...”",
    "GREEK": "πονηρός",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "ponēros",
    "HEBREW": "רַע",
    "HEBREW_TRANSLIT": "ra'",
    "OT_REFS": "Gen 6:5 • Ps 23:4 • Prov 8:13 • Isa 45:7",
    "NT_REFS": "Matt 6:13 • Rom 12:21 • 1 Thess 5:22 • 3 John 1:11",
    "TRIVIA_BULLETS": [
      "The Hebrew 'ra' encompasses both moral wickedness and physical calamity or disaster.",
      "Greek 'poneros' implies active, harmful evil, often personified as 'The Evil One' (Satan).",
      "In Isaiah 45:7, God 'creating evil' refers to His sovereignty over disaster and judgment, not sin."
